opennyai_summary.arguments:
When the claimants have come with a case, demanding higher amount of compensation, in that event, they have to produce evidence to that effect and have to lead evidence to show that, in fact, the market value of the acquired land is on much higher footing than the price determined by the Land Acquisition Officer.
It is an admitted position of fact that the burden of proof lies on the claimants to lead cogent and convincing evidence in support of their claim, which they have failed to establish in the present case despite sufficient opportunity being provided to them.
He has submitted that as per the statutory provisions of the Land Acquisition Act, within the span of six months from the NEUTRAL CITATION C/FA/878/2021 CAV JUDGMENT DATED: 20/07/2023 undefined date of order passed by the Collector and/or after receipt of notice from the Collector under Section 12(2) whichever is expired earlier, the reference is required to be filed.
The Land Acquisition Officer has declared the award on 04.08.2009 and the said award was passed in the absence of the claimants.
No evidence was laid by the respondent-authority to show that on which date notice under Section 12(2) of the Act was issued to the claimants.
The claimants have preferred the reference on 18.08.2009 and, therefore,
the document itself shows and suggests that the reference was preferred well within the time, i.e,
before the end of period of limitation.
