The law is well settled in that regard that considering the price rise of the property, 10% rise is required to be given to the subsequent date.
Therefore, at the most they are entitled to get 20% rise in the said amount as per the law laid down by the Hon'ble Apex Court in Maya Devi's case and, accordingly, price of the land is required to be fixed.
